{"type":"standard","title":"Brad Finstad","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Brad Finstad</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q111159803","titles":{"canonical":"Brad_Finstad","normalized":"Brad Finstad","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Brad Finstad</span></span>"},"pageid":70263550,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Rep._Brad_Finstad_%28R-MN%29%2C_Official_Portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg/330px-Rep._Brad_Finstad_%28R-MN%29%2C_Official_Portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":412},"originalimage":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Rep._Brad_Finstad_%28R-MN%29%2C_Official_Portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg/3840px-Rep._Brad_Finstad_%28R-MN%29%2C_Official_Portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":4824,"height":6029},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376027543","tid":"dca939b5-b5d3-11f1-b190-62c1c0f2ceb2","timestamp":"2026-09-21T15:48:17Z","description":"American politician (born 1976)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brad_Finstad","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brad_Finstad?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brad_Finstad?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Brad_Finstad"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brad_Finstad","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Brad_Finstad","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brad_Finstad?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Brad_Finstad"}},"extract":"Bradley Howard Finstad is an American politician serving since 2022 as the U.S. representative for Minnesota's 1st congressional district. Finstad represents a section of southern Minnesota along the border with Iowa. A member of the Republican Party, he served in the Minnesota House of Representatives from 2003 to 2009.","extract_html":"<p><b>Bradley Howard Finstad</b> is an American politician serving since 2022 as the U.S. representative for Minnesota's 1st congressional district. Finstad represents a section of southern Minnesota along the border with Iowa. A member of the Republican Party, he served in the Minnesota House of Representatives from 2003 to 2009.</p>"}